 "content": "# Translated motif copies\n\nUse this branch for a noisy grid containing a distinctive single-color motif amid zeros and another background color. Record the motif's colored-cell offsets from its bounding box. Search for translated copies whose motif positions all contain zeros, and recolor those matching positions with the motif color. Preserve every other cell, including the original motif and zeros/background at non-motif positions inside the bounding box. Do not assume flood-fill or neighbor propagation: test motif translations when the grid visually consists of noisy background plus one seed object. Account for legal translations within bounds; use rotation or reflection only when demonstrations support it.\n"
}

