 "content": "# Tile summary\n\nUse this branch when full-width and full-height separator lines partition the grid into equal tiles and the output dimensions match the tile layout. Map each tile to one output cell; use demonstrations to determine which in-tile feature or count controls that cell. Do not assume every unusual cell or a single marker is positive. For the demonstrated pattern with color-8 separators and 2×3 tiles containing mostly color 3 and occasional color 2, emit 1 for a tile with at least two 2s and 3 otherwise.\n"
}

{
 "path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/HA-openclaw-luna6-high-ws0/frozen/seen-4/play/users/u004/system/state/openclaw/agents/main/agent/workshop-skills/continual-arc/patterns/diagonal-stripes.md",
 "content": "# Diagonal stripes\n\nUse this branch for sparse colored diagonal markers on a zero field. Identify the invariant of their parallel lines: constant row−column for down-right diagonals, or row+column for down-left diagonals. Demonstrations may show that the output fills the whole grid with a periodic color sequence indexed by that invariant. Use zero-based row/column coordinates and verify the sign convention against observed output: for down-right stripes, `column−row` indexes the phase; for down-left stripes, `row+column` does. Infer the smallest plausible period by checking which candidate periods avoid assigning different colors to the same residue; use demo output to establish the complete mapping when available. Do not assume marker positions alone give every residue's color. Color every cell from its phase, then verify several cells against each demonstrated line and ensure the output reproduces every demo.\n"
}

